@startuml duplicate_record_evaluation
title Race condition em saveUserEvaluation() - avaliacoes duplicadas
autonumber

actor "Avaliador\n(Aba 1 / Sessao A)" as ClientA
actor "Avaliador\n(Aba 2 / Sessao B)" as ClientB
participant "PHP-FPM\n(Controller::POST_saveEvaluation)" as App
participant "Redis\n(session lock)" as Redis
participant "Registration\n(getUserEvaluation /\nsaveUserEvaluation)" as Entity
database "Postgres\n(registration_evaluation)" as DB

== Sessoes distintas: locks nao concorrem entre si ==

ClientA -> App: POST /saveEvaluation/{id}/status:evaluated\n(data.uid = X)
activate App
App -> Redis: session_start() lock(SESSID_A)
Redis --> App: lock adquirido

ClientB -> App: POST /saveEvaluation/{id}/status:evaluated\n(data.uid = X)
activate App
App -> Redis: session_start() lock(SESSID_B)
Redis --> App: lock adquirido (sessao diferente, sem espera)

== Janela de corrida (check-then-act sem lock de linha) ==

App -> Entity: saveUserEvaluation(data, uid=X)
activate Entity
Entity -> DB: SELECT * FROM registration_evaluation\nWHERE registration_id=R AND user_id=X
DB --> Entity: null (nenhuma linha encontrada)
note right of Entity #FFDDDD
  **getUserEvaluation()**
  Entities/Registration.php:1345
  findOneBy sem SELECT FOR UPDATE,
  sem transacao, sem lock
end note

App -> Entity: saveUserEvaluation(data, uid=X)
activate Entity #FFAAAA
Entity -> DB: SELECT * FROM registration_evaluation\nWHERE registration_id=R AND user_id=X
DB --> Entity: null (linha da 1a requisicao\nainda nao foi commitada)
note right of Entity #FFDDDD
  Mesma checagem, mesmo resultado:
  nenhuma avaliacao encontrada ainda
end note

Entity -> Entity: new RegistrationEvaluation()
Entity -> DB: INSERT INTO registration_evaluation (...)\n(saveEvaluation -> save(true))
DB --> Entity: OK, id = 179973
Entity --> App: evaluation #1
deactivate Entity
App --> ClientA: 200 OK
deactivate App

Entity -> Entity: new RegistrationEvaluation()
Entity -> DB: INSERT INTO registration_evaluation (...)\n(saveEvaluation -> save(true))
DB --> Entity: OK, id = 179974  **<< DUPLICATA**
Entity --> App: evaluation #2
deactivate Entity
App --> ClientB: 200 OK
deactivate App

note over DB #FFCCCC
  **Resultado:** 2 linhas para o mesmo
  (registration_id = R, user_id = X)
  => nota final calculada com dado duplicado
  (consolidateResult soma/considera ambas)
end note

== Por que nao reproduz na mesma sessao ==
note over ClientA, Redis #EEEEEE
  Se as 2 requisicoes vierem da MESMA sessao (mesmo PHPSESSID),
  o segundo session_start() fica bloqueado no lock do Redis ate
  o primeiro request terminar por completo (nao ha
  session_write_close() em nenhum lugar do App.php) - por isso
  o par de requests so serializa (create -> update) em vez de
  duplicar. Em producao, sob latencia, o lock do phpredis
  expira as tentativas e libera a 2a requisicao antes da 1a
  terminar, reabrindo a janela de corrida acima.
end note

@enduml
